Evaluator: A. Psaltis (04/2025)
Comments:
1. Resonance energies (corrected for nuclear masses) and spin/parities taken by Tilley et al. (1993)
and updated according to the latest AME.
2. Gamma_alpha assumed to have a factor uncertainty of 2.5 from 50% on the α-particle
spectroscopic factor from the transfer reaction and a factor of 2 uncertainty from the assumption of the mirror
symmetry (see also Mohr et al. 2014)
3. Gamma_p assumed to have 20% uncertainty when not given (factor uncertainty -1.2)
4. For the three directly measured resonances, Gamma_p and Gamma_alpha have same relative uncertainty as Gamma_tot
5. For the three directly measured resonances, Gamma_p = Gamma_p0
6. The direct capture S-factor has been calculated from the measurement of Jayatissa et al. (2022)
using their cross section data with increased uncertainty, due to the use of stopping power tables
7. For Er= 1932 and Er= 2252 keV, partial widths are taken from 16O(p,p), 16O(p,p') and 16O(p,a)13N measurements
8. The radius parameter was set to 1.9 fm to match the calculations form the work of Meyer et al. (2020)
